# Applies to the build above when BuildKit is used with
# `-f final-deliverable/Dockerfile`, keeping the exclusion list beside the
# Dockerfile it belongs to instead of at the repository root.
#
# The context is the repo root, which holds notebooks, a venv and a 580 KB
# image. Excluding them keeps the context small and, more importantly, keeps
# anything not named in a COPY out of reach of the build.
**/.git
**/.VENV
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/.ipynb_checkpoints

# Analysis and authoring material: not part of the runtime.
notebooks/
notebook-590/
presentations/
*.jpg
*.png

# Raw connector extracts. Only data/processed/ and the one manual file are
# COPYed; the raw .toon/.json inputs belong to the build pipeline, not the
# serving image.
data/raw/

# This directory's own non-runtime files.
final-deliverable/tests/
final-deliverable/scripts/
final-deliverable/README.md
final-deliverable/Makefile
final-deliverable/docker-compose.yml
final-deliverable/requirements-dev.txt
